# This repository follows its own advice (see docs/hardening.md).
#
# Never run dependency lifecycle scripts (preinstall/install/postinstall/prepare) on install: install-time
# execution is how Shai-Hulud-style worms run. Every CI job also passes --ignore-scripts explicitly.
# Side effect: npm skips pre/post scripts too (e.g. prepack), so CI runs "npm run build" before "npm pack".
ignore-scripts=true
# Refuse to resolve versions published less than 7 days ago: the default soak `wormsign soak` enforces. This
# cooldown only checks age and never reads advisories, so what it relies on is removal. Per
# docs/evidence/soak-latency.md a public malware advisory listed 99.9% of measured worm versions within 72 hours,
# but removal from npm could be proven within 72 hours for only 49.2% of them (51.3% within 7 days: the data shows
# 72 hours is not enough on its own, not how much 7 days adds).
# Needs npm >= 11.10 (Node 24 bundles npm 11): npm 10, bundled with Node 22, reads this key and silently ignores
# it. It also does not stop `npm ci` installing a version that is already locked, so the lockfile is gated
# separately by `wormsign soak` in .github/workflows/wormsign.yml.
min-release-age=7
